# Example hostname to library identifier map, for use with an Apache
# RewriteMap.  See the "Apache Rewrite Tricks" chapter of the Evergreen
# documentation, the commented example virtual host in eg.conf, and
# libphysloc.txt.example.
#
# Apache splits each line on whitespace: the first field is the key, the
# second is the value.  Lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
# Look the hostname up in lower case (see the "lowercase" internal map in
# the eg.conf example), so that the table needs only one entry per host.
#
# The identifiers below are org unit shortnames from the Concerto sample
# data set.  Several hostnames may share an identifier.  Hostnames that are
# not listed fall back to the default supplied by the RewriteRule, which in
# the shipped example is the CONS consortium.

br1.evergreen.local     BR1
br2.evergreen.local     BR2
br3.evergreen.local     BR3
br4.evergreen.local     BR4
sys1.evergreen.local    SYS1
sys2.evergreen.local    SYS2
